{"title":"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay A Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> below with the number that you receive.\n</p><p>The diagram shows a white rectangle inside a shaded rectangle.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The white rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b680ba39a27829b28b2f6c74b37f8fad6056de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\text { m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957c7e3cde7b0cb5da528548005924699ba1003e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 \\text { m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" /> and the shaded rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/d/c2dfe8343d045eebe61788da37f103b0b59c9de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\text { m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/7/5a7f3da88a9e5f02565c80a95f402445176f5cc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\text { m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. What is the area of the shaded region, in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e134066861513d827b5750f9e4e6a7a47bfcfee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{m}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the area of the shaded region would just be the area of the inner unshaded region subtracted from the total area of the whole rectangle.\n</p><p>The area of a rectangle is its width multiplied by its height. This means that the area of the inner unshaded region would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/2/7022b522130eef1ede7692078c4020519e8273a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 \\times 10 = 300 \\text{ m}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Applying this to the whole rectangle, its area would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2f5a7970de8c5dc4de2ca94d513fbf20eb9bfe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20N \\text{ m}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>The area of the shaded region would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f76d0556073ba0acfa2963eceed197ec8d095a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20N - 300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e134066861513d827b5750f9e4e6a7a47bfcfee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{m}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay A Problem 3\">player 3</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/c/97c0c2331d768e3cf2ec036a99778f5bfe78c3f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The area of the shaded region is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/7/467de5dc46884886bc90a13d252698fb782667e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\times 60 - 300 = 1200 - 300 = \\boxed{900 \\text{ m}^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"310\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC\">2024 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay A Problem 3\">Relay A Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 1\">Relay B Problem 1</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Proble